gfs2: Fix "gfs2: Switch to wait_event in gfs2_quotad"

jira KERNEL-1773
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.176.1.el8_10
commit-author Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
commit dff1fb6d8b7abe5b1119fa060f5d6b3370bf10ac
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.176.1.el8_10/dff1fb6d.failed

Commit e4a8b5481c59a ("gfs2: Switch to wait_event in gfs2_quotad") broke
cyclic statfs syncing, so the numbers reported by "df" could easily get
completely out of sync with reality.  Fix this by reverting part of
commit e4a8b5481c59a for now.

A follow-up commit will clean this code up later.

	Signed-off-by: Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit dff1fb6d8b7abe5b1119fa060f5d6b3370bf10ac)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/gfs2/quota.c
diff --cc fs/gfs2/quota.c
index 6caaa00aaf67,f2df01f801b8..000000000000
--- a/fs/gfs2/quota.c
+++ b/fs/gfs2/quota.c
@@@ -1594,13 -1614,11 +1594,17 @@@ int gfs2_quotad(void *data
  		quotad_check_timeo(sdp, "sync", gfs2_quota_sync, t,
  				   &quotad_timeo, &tune->gt_quota_quantum);
  
 +		try_to_freeze();
 +
  		t = min(quotad_timeo, statfs_timeo);
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +		t = wait_event_interruptible_timeout(sdp->sd_quota_wait,
++=======
+ 		t -= wait_event_freezable_timeout(sdp->sd_quota_wait,
++>>>>>>> dff1fb6d8b7a (gfs2: Fix "gfs2: Switch to wait_event in gfs2_quotad")
  				sdp->sd_statfs_force_sync ||
 -				gfs2_withdrawing_or_withdrawn(sdp) ||
 +				gfs2_withdrawn(sdp) ||
  				kthread_should_stop(),
  				t);
  
* Unmerged path fs/gfs2/quota.c
